    {
      "id": "sum-af69b5",
      "kind": "controversy",
      "body": "Issue #3244, still open, challenges the phrase 'sanitizing potentially dangerous characters'. jmanico argues sanitization is the wrong SSRF control and should be dropped; tghosth has endorsed that direction. elarlang then asked how the remainder differs from V13.2.4. Two proposals are in play: fold user-input SSRF into V13.2.4 and remove V1.3.6, or keep a first-layer application allowlist here and a second-layer infrastructure allowlist in V13.2.4. No wording change has been merged.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "issue_body",
          "url": "https://github.com/OWASP/ASVS/issues/3244",
          "issue": 3244
        }
      ],
